messages.content:
New medication: amiodarone. Patient active medications: warfarin, lisinopril, atorvastatin.

Verified interaction findings from the formulary reference:
{
  "new_drug": "amiodarone",
  "pairs_checked": [
    "amiodarone + warfarin",
    "amiodarone + lisinopril",
    "amiodarone + atorvastatin"
  ],
  "significant_findings": [
    {
      "pair": "amiodarone + warfarin",
      "severity": "major",
      "mechanism": "Amiodarone inhibits CYP2C9 and P-glycoprotein, reducing warfarin clearance and markedly raising INR and bleeding risk.",
      "management": "Empirically reduce the warfarin dose ~30-50% when starting amiodarone and monitor INR closely for several weeks."
    },
    {
      "pair": "amiodarone + atorvastatin",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "mechanism": "Amiodarone inhibits CYP3A4, increasing atorvastatin exposure and the risk of myopathy/rhabdomyolysis.",
      "management": "Use the lowest effective statin dose and counsel on muscle pain/weakness; consider a statin less dependent on CYP3A4."
    }
  ],
  "source": "hospital formulary interaction reference (on-prem)"
}

Give the medication-safety assessment.
